@baseUrl = http://localhost:3000
@token = REPLACE_WITH_A_REAL_TOKEN
@tokenNoDeleteScope = REPLACE_WITH_A_TOKEN_MISSING_DELETE_SCOPE
@tokenExcludedDeck = REPLACE_WITH_A_TOKEN_THAT_EXCLUDES_deckId_BELOW
@tokenNoSchemaDelete = REPLACE_WITH_A_TOKEN_ON_A_ROLE_WITH_canDelete_FALSE

### =========================================================================
### 1) SUCCESS — empty deck (no cards, no nested decks, no connections)
### =========================================================================
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/table
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "name": "DeleteDeckEmpty"
}

###
@emptyDeckId = 00000000-0000-0000-0000-000000000000

### → 200, { data: { deleted: true, mediaPurged: 0, mediaFailed: 0 } }
DELETE {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/table/{{emptyDeckId}}
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}

### 2) same deck again → 404 NOT_FOUND (already gone)
DELETE {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/table/{{emptyDeckId}}
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}

### =========================================================================
### 3) NODE_HAS_CHILDREN — deck with a nested card, no ?cascade
### =========================================================================
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/table
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "name": "DeleteDeckWithCard"
}

###
@deckWithCardId = 00000000-0000-0000-0000-000000000000

### setup: one card inside it
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/card
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "name": "SomeCard",
  "parentId": "{{deckWithCardId}}",
  "fieldType": "text"
}

### 3a) delete without cascade → 409 { error: "NODE_HAS_CHILDREN", count: 1, message: "...Pass ?cascade=true..." }
DELETE {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/table/{{deckWithCardId}}
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}

### 3b) delete with ?cascade=true → 200, deletes the deck and its card together
DELETE {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/table/{{deckWithCardId}}?cascade=true
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}

### =========================================================================
### 4) NODE_HAS_CHILDREN — deck with a NESTED SUB-DECK (not just a card)
### =========================================================================
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/table
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "name": "DeleteDeckWithSubdeck"
}

###
@deckWithSubdeckId = 00000000-0000-0000-0000-000000000000

### setup: nested sub-deck
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/table
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "name": "NestedSubdeck",
  "parentId": "{{deckWithSubdeckId}}"
}

### 4a) delete without cascade → 409 NODE_HAS_CHILDREN, count: 1 (the sub-deck)
DELETE {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/table/{{deckWithSubdeckId}}
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}

### 4b) delete with ?cascade=true → 200, deletes the whole subtree
DELETE {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/table/{{deckWithSubdeckId}}?cascade=true
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}

### =========================================================================
### 5) MEDIA CLEANUP — cascade-deleting a deck purges every media file its
### cards uploaded (mediaPurged reflects the real count, mediaFailed stays 0
### unless a storage delete actually errored)
### =========================================================================
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/table
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "name": "DeleteDeckWithMedia"
}

###
@deckWithMediaId = 00000000-0000-0000-0000-000000000000

### setup: image card with a real base64 upload
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/card
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "name": "FotoConMedia",
  "parentId": "{{deckWithMediaId}}",
  "fieldType": "image",
  "config": {
    "base64": "iVBORw0KGgoAAAANSUhEUgAAAAEAAAABCAQAAAC1HAwCAAAAC0lEQVR42mNk+A8AAQUBAScY42YAAAAASUVORK5CYII=",
    "mimeType": "image/png",
    "filename": "foto.png"
  }
}

### → 200, { data: { deleted: true, mediaPurged: 1, mediaFailed: 0 } }
DELETE {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/table/{{deckWithMediaId}}?cascade=true
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}

### =========================================================================
### 6) NODE_HAS_CONNECTIONS — NOT RUNNABLE from this file.
### A "connection" (vínculo) between two decks is only created from the CMS
### board UI (drag a relation between two mazos), the public v1 API has no
### endpoint that creates one. Documented for completeness:
###
### DELETE {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/table/{deckId}   (deck has ≥1 active connection, no ?cascade)
### → 409 { error: "NODE_HAS_CONNECTIONS", count: <n>,
###         message: "...has <n> active relation(s)...Pass ?cascade=true..." }
###
### DELETE {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/table/{deckId}?cascade=true
### → 200, deletes the deck (and its connections) anyway.
### =========================================================================

### =========================================================================
### 7) BAD REQUEST / NOT FOUND — malformed or wrong-type ids
### =========================================================================

### 7a) non-UUID deckId → 404 NOT_FOUND (isUuid guard)
DELETE {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/table/not-a-uuid
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}

### 7b) well-formed UUID that never existed → 404 NOT_FOUND
DELETE {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/table/11111111-1111-1111-1111-111111111111
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}

### 7c) setup: a plain card, to pass its id where a deckId is expected
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/table
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "name": "DeleteDeckTypeCheck"
}

###
@typeCheckDeckId = 00000000-0000-0000-0000-000000000000

POST {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/card
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "name": "NotADeck",
  "parentId": "{{typeCheckDeckId}}",
  "fieldType": "text"
}

###
@notADeckCardId = 00000000-0000-0000-0000-000000000000

### 7d) a card id passed to the deck-delete endpoint → 400 BAD_REQUEST "Node is not a deck."
DELETE {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/table/{{notADeckCardId}}
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}

### cleanup for this section
DELETE {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/table/{{typeCheckDeckId}}?cascade=true
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}

### =========================================================================
### 8) AUTH — missing/invalid Authorization → 401 UNAUTHORIZED
### =========================================================================
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/table
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "name": "DeleteDeckAuthCheck"
}

###
@authCheckDeckId = 00000000-0000-0000-0000-000000000000

### 8a) no Authorization header at all
DELETE {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/table/{{authCheckDeckId}}

### 8b) unknown/garbage token
DELETE {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/table/{{authCheckDeckId}}
Authorization: Bearer this-token-does-not-exist

### =========================================================================
### 9) SCOPE — token has no "delete" scope → 403 FORBIDDEN
### Generate @tokenNoDeleteScope in Settings → API with scope = ["read","write","update"]
### =========================================================================
DELETE {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/table/{{authCheckDeckId}}
Authorization: Bearer {{tokenNoDeleteScope}}

### =========================================================================
### 10) TOKEN POLICY — this deckId is in the token's excluded list → 403 FORBIDDEN
### Generate @tokenExcludedDeck in Settings → API excluding {{authCheckDeckId}} explicitly
### =========================================================================
DELETE {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/table/{{authCheckDeckId}}
Authorization: Bearer {{tokenExcludedDeck}}

### =========================================================================
### 11) ROLE — token's role has schema canDelete = false → 403 FORBIDDEN
### Generate @tokenNoSchemaDelete on a role whose Settings → Roles schema
### permissions have "Delete card/deck" unchecked for this project
### =========================================================================
DELETE {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/table/{{authCheckDeckId}}
Authorization: Bearer {{tokenNoSchemaDelete}}

### cleanup for section 8/9/10/11 (only succeeds once a valid full-scope token is used)
DELETE {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/table/{{authCheckDeckId}}?cascade=true
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}
